descriptions.job-15g61q2:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Agentic payments is a team that’s building new APIs and integration experiences for agentic commerce online. We think that the proliferation of consumer-facing AI experiences will unlock new ways that consumers buy things online, and our existing payments experiences need to evolve to new commercial models that cutting-edge builders are starting. Our first launch, Instant Checkout in collaboration with OpenAI, took the industry by storm and we’re bringing experiences like that to the entire universe of AI agents and sellers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager on Agentic Commerce, you’ll own the shaping and delivery of transformative products that redefine how commerce works, making it more fluid, automated, and aligned with user intent. You’ll collaborate closely with product management, design, data science, and marketing to unlock new opportunities for our customers and partners globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our north star provides a new integration model for AI agents who are looking to build agent-powered online commerce experiences, via their Stripe integration. They will have access to our entire suite of connected sellers, and can focus on the end-user experience. Enabling an AI agent to do this requires new API primitives, new dashboard surfaces, and deep thought about what financial and e-commerce complexity Stripe can simplify on their behalf.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build full stack solutions across Stripe&#39;s ecosystem, including back end services, dashboard interfaces, money movement systems, and integrations with other Stripe primitives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner deeply with product management and design to ship high impact features that increase user autonomy and reduce friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply strong analytical skills to dive into data, test hypotheses, and make informed trade-offs. Set success metrics for the team to ensure solutions are enterprise-grade and quickly meet Stripe’s reliability SLOs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally across Stripe’s broader platform and product teams to integrate agentic commerce capabilities seamlessly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with users (particularly large enterprises) to understand their business needs and translate requirements into novel product shapes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of engineering experience with a computer science background with hands on development expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native and very comfortable autonomously solving problems with agentic AI tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience coaching and developing senior and staff level individual contributors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience of leading initiatives that touch large engineering organizations, spanning multiple teams to influence tech roadmap planning and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, structuring ambiguous concepts clearly and from first principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in a collaborative environment involving different functions, stakeholders, and subject matter experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep empathy for users balancing autonomy and guidance in digital commerce experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of engineering management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building APIs or new integration experiences for users, several of them being enterprise grade&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve been on the founding team of a business / startup, taking a product from 0-1&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in eCommerce and/or payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

descriptions.job-1sawd6i:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Grayscale is the largest digital asset-focused investment platform in the world by AUM and offers the broadest selection of digital asset investment products in the U.S. based on number of products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our platform spans the full spectrum of institutional-grade solutions—from single-asset exposures to diversified and thematic strategies—with a goal of providing every investor with access to the hyper-expanding digital asset universe. &amp;nbsp;Our firm offers a rare combination of decades of traditional finance work experience and digital asset leadership that brings an institutional mindset to the maturing digital asset industry. This convergence of capabilities positions us to deliver investment solutions and client experiences that are both institutionally robust and technologically advanced, which we believe offers a competitive edge that is difficult to replicate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proud of our deep crypto expertise and work closely with individual and institutional investors as they explore this asset class as part of their portfolio allocation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Grayscale is seeking a Staff DevSecOps engineer to join our Engineering team. You will own the DevOps, SecOps, cloud governance, and infrastructure architecture that underpins all of Grayscale&#39;s technology delivery. This is a shared enabling role. Your work will make delivery faster by making it safer, more observable, and more repeatable for other squads. You will partner closely with engineering leads, security, and architecture to build a modern, well-governed cloud environment. This role reports into the Head of Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech Stack:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We utilize AWS as our cloud platform, enabling scalable and secure infrastructure. Our infrastructure is managed using Terraform, with Docker and AWS Lambda and Fargate for containerization and deployment. We rely on GitLab for our CI/CD processes. There is significant opportunity to modernize our cloud posture, accelerate developer productivity, and formalize DevSecOps practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain cloud infrastructure on AWS using Terraform, Docker, and related IaC tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve CI/CD pipelines in GitLab to ensure smooth, secure, and efficient software delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain DevSecOps practices including security scanning, vulnerability management, and compliance automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and enforce cloud governance policies, cost management, and architectural guardrails across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build observability and monitoring solutions that improve reliability, performance, and incident response across all platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the security team to ensure ITGC evidence, audit readiness, and control frameworks are in place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accelerate developer productivity through self-service tooling, environment automation, and standardized deployment patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure high-quality infrastructure delivery through strong collaboration with product, engineering, and security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set architecture standards and technical direction for cloud and delivery, in coordination with engineering leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on industry trends and emerging technologies in cloud infrastructure, DevOps, and platform engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers across the organization on infrastructure, cloud architecture, and operational excellence, acting as a leverage point for work you do not personally deliver&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in platform engineering, DevOps, or infrastructure roles with deep AWS experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable track record of setting technical direction that others adopted: a pattern, standard, or platform used beyond your own project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, or a related field, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with Infrastructure-as-Code tools (Terraform, CloudFormation, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with containerization (Docker, ECS/EKS) and serverless architectures (Lambda, Step Functions).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in CI/CD pipeline design and management, preferably with GitLab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of DevSecOps practices, security scanning, and compliance automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of cloud governance, cost optimization, and architectural best practices on AWS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate business and engineering needs into infrastructure solutions and platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Agile proficiency with practical application to deliver incremental, high-quality solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and communication skills, capable of influencing both technical and business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage complex project timelines in fast-paced environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a regulated industry and/or Financial Services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills, adept at building collaborative relationships across teams and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS certifications (Preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

descriptions.job-0bdwcsa:
&lt;p&gt;It all started with an idea at Block in 2013. Initially built to take the pain out of peer-to-peer payments, Cash App has gone from a simple product with a single purpose to a dynamic ecosystem, developing unique financial products, including Afterpay/Clearpay, to provide a better way to send, spend, invest, borrow and save to our 50+ million monthly active customers. We want to redefine the world’s relationship with money to make it more relatable, instantly available, and universally accessible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, Cash App has thousands of employees working globally across office and remote locations, with a culture geared toward innovation, collaboration and impact. We’ve been a distributed team since day one, and many of our roles can be done remotely from the countries where Cash App operates. No matter the location, we tailor our experience to ensure our employees are creative, productive, and happy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The North American Mid-Market Sales team at Cash App and Afterpay is responsible for driving revenue across our commerce payments products, giving merchant partners access to one of the largest and most engaged networks of next-generation consumers. We partner with high-growth and established brands across retail, fashion, beauty, travel, QSR, home, health and wellness, ticketing, and other commerce categories to help them acquire customers, increase conversion, and grow profitably.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced Mid-Market Account Executive to build and expand relationships with high-potential merchants across North America. You will own a portfolio of prospective merchants, create new pipeline, lead a consultative sales process, and close new business across Cash App Pay and Afterpay.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work with founders, executives, and leaders across commerce, marketing, payments, finance, and technology. Internally, you will coordinate partners across Product, Engineering, Marketing, Finance, Legal, Risk, Sales Strategy, and Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will independently own complex sales workstreams, make informed tradeoffs, and influence deal strategy and execution within your area of responsibility. Success requires balancing high-touch relationship development with a structured and repeatable sales process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a portfolio of mid-market opportunities from initial prospecting and qualification through discovery, negotiation, contracting, launch, and handoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop account plans that identify merchant priorities, key decision-makers, potential blockers, and revenue opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build pipeline through outbound outreach, market research, internal lead assignments, vertical insights, events, referrals, and partner introductions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualify and prioritize opportunities based on merchant fit, revenue potential, product alignment, implementation requirements, and likelihood to close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery with business and technical stakeholders to understand merchant priorities, customer needs, payment flows, and implementation requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build merchant-specific business cases and sales narratives that connect Cash App Pay and Afterpay’s capabilities to customer acquisition, conversion, and growth goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop commercial proposals and negotiate pricing, financial terms, contracts, procurement requirements, and implementation dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate deal teams across Product, Engineering, Marketing, Finance, Legal, Risk, Sales Strategy, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage deal progress using defined milestones, next steps, stakeholder ownership, and internal approval requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate opportunity data, pipeline reporting, and sales forecasts in Salesforce and related systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring merchant feedback, competitive intelligence, and market insights back to Product and go-to-market teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to sales processes, enablement materials, and operating rhythms that improve pipeline quality, deal velocity, forecast accuracy, and win rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver against individual revenue and sales targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Cash App and Afterpay in merchant meetings, industry events, and networking forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in full-cycle B2B sales, business development, partnerships, or a related go-to-market role, preferably in commerce, payments, fintech, SaaS, retail technology, or another fast-moving technology environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrated track record of meeting or exceeding quota and closing mid-market or complex commercial deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong prospecting and pipeline-generation skills, including comfort building new business through outbound outreach, market research, partner referrals, events, and executive networking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence with the ability to earn trust, ask strong questions, influence senior stakeholders, and tailor communication to founders, functional leaders, and cross-functional buying committees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial judgment and negotiation skills, including comfort working through pricing, legal terms, procurement, implementation dependencies, and internal approval processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort using data to build a business case, prioritize opportunities, inspect pipeline quality, and communicate tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product curiosity and technical fluency, especially around payments, commerce, customer acquisition, marketing, and merchant growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter mentality and comfort operating through ambiguity, frequent change, and evolving priorities while still delivering results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional collaboration skills and the ability to lead workstreams without formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to build concise, compelling narratives for internal and external audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A continuous-improvement mindset and willingness to help build better team processes, enablement materials, and operating rhythms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to travel for merchant meetings, industry events, and internal team moments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Block takes a market-based approach to pay, and pay may vary depending on your location. U.S. locations are categorized into one of four zones based on a cost of labor index for that geographic area. The successful candidate&#39;s starting pay will be determined based on job-related skills, experience, qualifications, work location, and market conditions. These ranges may be modified in the future. To find a location&#39;s zone designation, please refer to this&lt;a href=&quot;https://block.xyz/documents/salaryzones.pdf&quot;&gt; resource&lt;/a&gt;. If a location of interest is not listed, please speak with a recruiter for additional information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zone A: $217,840.00 - $326,760.00&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Zone B: $202,560.00 - $303,840.00&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zone C: $191,680.00 - $287,520.00&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Zone D: $185,200.00 -$277,800.00 &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amounts listed above include target variable compensation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We’re working to build a more inclusive economy where our customers have equal access to opportunity, and we strive to live by these same values in building our workplace. Block is an equal opportunity employer evaluating all employees and job applicants without regard to identity or any legally protected class. We will consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records for employment in accordance with state and local laws and “fair chance” ordinances.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We believe in being fair, and are committed to an inclusive interview experience, including providing reasonable accommodations to disabled applicants throughout the recruitment process. We encourage applicants to share any needed accommodations with their recruiter, who will treat these requests as confidentially as possible. &lt;strong&gt;Want to learn more about what we’re doing to build a workplace that is fair and square? Check out our&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://block.xyz/news/inclusion&quot;&gt;I+D page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While there is no specific deadline to apply for this role, U.S. roles are typically open for an average of 55 days before being filled by a successful candidate. Please refer to the date listed at the top of this job page for when this role was first posted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Guidelines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates may submit up to 9 active applications within a 60-day period. Reapplications to the same role are accepted 90 days after a previous application has been reviewed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use of AI in Our Hiring Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We may use automated AI tools to evaluate job applications for efficiency and consistency. These tools comply with local regulations, including bias audits, and we handle all personal data in accordance with state and local privacy laws.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contact us &lt;a href=&quot;https://privacy.block.xyz/privacyportal/form&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;with hiring practice or data usage questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Every benefit we offer is designed with one goal: empowering you to do the best work of your career while building the life you want. Remote work, medical insurance, flexible time off, retirement savings plans, and modern family planning are just some of our offering.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://block.xyz/employee-benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://block.xyz/documents/benefits.pdf&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Check out our other benefits at Block.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Block, Inc. (NYSE: XYZ) builds technology to increase access to the global economy. Each of our brands unlocks different aspects of the economy for more people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Square&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;makes commerce and financial services accessible to sellers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Cash App&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is the easy way to spend, send, and store money.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Afterpay&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is transforming the way customers manage their spending over time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;TIDAL&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a music platform that empowers artists to thrive as entrepreneurs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Bitkey&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a simple self-custody wallet built for bitcoin.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Proto&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a suite of bitcoin mining products and services. Together, we’re helping build a financial system that is open to everyone.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://block.xyz/en/legal/applicant-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

descriptions.job-15daipm:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team + role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems. We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood Ventures’ mission is to build one of the best venture capital platforms in the world and make it accessible to investors everywhere. Through our publicly-traded funds in Robinhood Ventures Fund I and Robinhood Ventures Fund II&amp;nbsp; we’ve already invested in some of the best private companies in the world like OpenAI, Databricks, Ramp, and more - and we’re just getting started.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Investment Intern in Robinhood Ventures you will be a core part of our lean team. You will research, evaluate, and support investments across the Robinhood Ventures platform, with a focus on late-stage investments.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Menlo Park, CA office with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Research and sourcing &lt;/strong&gt;- You’ll research markets and sectors that you believe we should be paying attention to, and then identify the key companies in them that Robinhood Ventures needs to meet.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investment evaluation &lt;/strong&gt;- You’ll be a key part of the deal team for investments we evaluate. You’ll own core diligence workstreams like the financial model, competitive analysis, and help shape investment theses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform building &lt;/strong&gt;- You’ll work with teams across Product, Operations, Marketing, Legal, and more to help build experiences in the Robinhood app to further differentiate Robinhood Ventures for both retail investors and portfolio companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently enrolled in a full-time MBA program&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in investment banking, private equity, or finance at a high-growth company, with fluency in financial modeling, valuation analysis, and market research; late-stage investing or venture capital experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intellectual curiosity and a demonstrated interest in emerging technologies and the private companies driving them — you proactively form opinions on key trends and companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An existing network in the startup ecosystem, or the drive to build one, that can help Robinhood Ventures identify and connect with promising companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work independently in lean, high-output environments, with experience collaborating across cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we offer&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market competitive compensation structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quarterly lifestyle wallet for personal wellness, learning and development, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to the best AI tools on the market and continuous AI skill-building for every employee, technical or not&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time away including company holidays, paid time off, and sick time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lively office environment with catered meals, fully stocked kitchens, and geo-specific commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot; data-sheets-value=&quot;{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;The expected salary range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. This role is also eligible to participate in a Robinhood bonus plan.\n\nUS Zone 1: $24.65 - $29 per hour\nUS Zone 2: $24.65 - $29 per hour\nUS Zone 3: $23.8 - $28 per hour&amp;quot;}&quot; data-sheets-userformat=&quot;{&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:4540,&amp;quot;5&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:[{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;5&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0}},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;3&amp;quot;:3},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;4&amp;quot;:1}]},&amp;quot;6&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:[{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;5&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0}},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;3&amp;quot;:3},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;4&amp;quot;:1}]},&amp;quot;7&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:[{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;5&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0}},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;3&amp;quot;:3},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;4&amp;quot;:1}]},&amp;quot;8&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:[{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;5&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0}},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;3&amp;quot;:3},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;4&amp;quot;:1}]},&amp;quot;10&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;11&amp;quot;:4,&amp;quot;15